    "teacher_markdown": "**What Students Should Take Away:**\r\n\r\n- Students use `groupby()` and `size()` to calculate the overall number of passengers in each survival category.\r\n- Students recognize that the stacked bar chart compares survival across passenger classes, while the pie chart shows the overall survival distribution.\r\n- Students use evidence from both visualizations to develop a more complete answer to the data question.\r\n\r\n**Misconceptions Students Might Have or Points They Might Struggle With and Tips to Assist:**\r\n\r\n- Students may think the pie chart shows survival within each passenger class.\r\n  - Tip: Reinforce that the pie chart combines passengers from all classes into one overall distribution.\r\n- Students may reverse the labels for the `0` and `1` survival values.\r\n  - Tip: Remind students that `0` means did not survive and `1` means survived. The label order must match the order of `survival_counts`.\r\n- Students may assume the overall percentages describe every class equally.\r\n  - Tip: Have students compare the overall pie chart with each class in the stacked bar chart. AI Tutor can help explain the code or chart output without answering the data question.",
    "display_name": "Titanic Survival",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Practice creating a **pie chart** to continue to answer a question about the Titanic!",
